{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.DeuteronFusionFrame","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.DeuteronFusionFrame","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.barOdd_of_barEven_mul_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.barOdd_of_barEven_mul_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L164-L174","doc":"**Parity of a product (bookkeeping).** bar-even × bar-odd is bar-odd.\nSo the deuteron law `B = (5g)·E_unit` has `B` bar-odd iff `E_unit` is\nbar-odd (`5g` is bar-even). Which parity `B(²H)` actually carries is an\n*empirical* question, currently open: the reeb-flow §2h data have the\nbar-**even** `2mₑ` closest (+2.6 %) and the bar-**odd** `𝔔_β` worst\n(−21 %), weakly favoring a bar-even unit — so this lemma is neutral\nbookkeeping, not a claim that `B(²H)` is bar-odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.barEven_ne_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.barEven_ne_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L151-L162","doc":"**A nonzero bar-even quantity is never bar-odd** (char ≠ 2). Hence the\nbar-even `E_unit` cannot equal the bar-odd `𝔔_β`: the entire bar-odd\ntransition sector is excluded as the deuteron unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.barEven_of_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.barEven_of_mul","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L140-L149","doc":"**A quotient of bar-even quantities is bar-even.** If `E·s = B` with `B`\nand `s` bar-even and `s ≠ 0`, then `E` is bar-even. Applied to\n`B = 5g·E_unit`: `B` (binding) and `5g` are bar-even, so `E_unit` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.BarOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.BarOdd","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L137-L138","doc":"Bar-odd: negated by the involution (𝔔_β / sinh decay channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.BarEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.BarEven","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L134-L135","doc":"Bar-even: fixed by the involution (binding / cosh channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.deformation_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.deformation_split","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L111-L120","doc":"**The two deformations split by exactly `1 + x/5`.** Cross-multiplied\nform of `(1/g)² / (5g)² = (5 + x)² / 25`: the fully-deformed `1/g` and\nthe classical-count `5g` coincide at `x = 0` (v = 1) and separate at\nfirst order in the deformation parameter `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.five_g_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.five_g_closed","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L100-L109","doc":"**`5g` in closed form (deformation (i)).** At criticality the exchange\nrate satisfies `g²·(5 + x) = 1` with `x = (v − v⁻¹)²` (compose\n`criticality_reciprocal` with `five_plus_x`). Then the squared binding\nmagnitude obeys `(5g)²·(5 + x) = 25` — the radical-free form of\n`5g = 5/√(5 + x)`. The reeb-flow §2e correction ladder\n`√5·(1 − x/10 + 3x²/200 − x³/400 − ⋯)` is exactly the Taylor expansion\nof this closed form (coefficients recorded in the D4 witness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.deformation_ii_eq_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.deformation_ii_eq_inv","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L91-L98","doc":"**Deformation (ii) = 1/g.** The fully-deformed candidate `s·g` equals\n`g⁻¹` whenever `g²·s = 1` — so the two canonical deformations of the\nclassical 5, namely `5g` and `(1 + [2]_v²)·g`, are the criticality pair\n`5g` and `1/g`, split by the exact factor `(1 + [2]_v²)/5 = 1 + x/5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.criticality_reciprocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.criticality_reciprocal","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L80-L89","doc":"**Criticality = normalized channel projection.** With `t = [2]_v` and\nthe squared rate `g²` defined by `g²·(1 + z²) = z²` for `z = 1/t` (i.e.\n`g² = z²/(1+z²)` cleared of its outer division), one has `g²·(1 + t²) = 1`:\nthe landed magnitude is exactly the marginal-stability point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.linking_rate_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.linking_rate_sq","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L67-L78","doc":"**Linking rate², geometry-independent (the radical-free core of D3).**\nFor a slope `z = n·r/R` geodesic pair on a torus with cycle\ncircumferences `(c·R, c·r)` (`c = 2π`), the squared linking rate\n`(|Lk|·c·r)² / L²`, `L² = (c·R)²(1+z²)`, equals `z²/(1+z²)` — the 2π\nand the individual radii cancel; only the slope survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.total_dim_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.total_dim_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L62-L65","doc":"Sanity: at v = 1 the total quantum dimension is exactly 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.five_plus_x","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.five_plus_x","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L54-L60","doc":"**The classical 5.** 1 + [2]_v² = 5 + (v − v⁻¹)², so at v = 1 the\ntotal quantum dimension of the two-nucleon channel decomposition is 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.fusion_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.fusion_identity","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L46-L52","doc":"**Fusion identity** [2]_v² = [3]_v + 1 — the quantum-dimension form of\nthe spin coupling ½ ⊗ ½ = 1 ⊕ 0. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:deuteron-fusion-frame","label":"prop:deuteron-fusion-frame","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.threeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.threeV","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L43-L44","doc":"Symmetric q-integer [3]_v = v² + 1 + v⁻². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.twoV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronFusion.twoV","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-fusion-frame.lean#L40-L41","doc":"Symmetric q-integer [2]_v = v + v⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0}]}